---
source: tests/it/cli_config.rs
expression: text(&out.stdout)
---
Render a Markdown document, or show an image, in the terminal

Usage: kiri [OPTIONS] [FILE]...

Arguments:
  [FILE]...  Markdown, CSV or TSV, an image, a Mermaid diagram, or a directory

Options:
      --doctor                  Show what kiri finds out about the terminal, for a bug report
      --list-emojis             List the emoji shortcodes, such as :smile:
      --raw                     With --doctor: the report as Markdown, also in a terminal
      --format <FORMAT>         What the file is, such as markdown, csv or png
      --width <WIDTH>           Width in cells; defaults to the terminal width
      --mode <MODE>             Which terminal features to use [default: auto] [possible values:
                                auto, plain, ansi, kitty]
      --theme <THEME>           Theme file, or a theme's name
      --light                   A light page in greys, as --theme light
      --dark                    A dark page in greys, as --theme dark
  -M, --no-margins              No margins, indents or padding, for copying text
      --margins                 Keep the margins, whatever KIRI_MARGINS and the configuration say
  -I, --no-images               Show images as their alt text and diagrams as code
      --images                  Show images, whatever KIRI_NO_IMAGES and the configuration say
      --paging <WHEN>           When to show the document in the pager [possible values: always,
                                auto, never]
  -p                            Show the document in the pager: --paging=always
  -P                            Print the document without the pager: --paging=never
      --follow <WHEN>           Follow a lone file in the pager [possible values: on, off, auto]
  -f                            Follow the file, in the pager: --follow=on
      --fa                      Follow the file and move to a change: --follow=auto
  -F                            Do not follow the file: --follow=off
      --follow-jump <WHICH>     Which change auto-follow moves the view to [possible values: first,
                                last, most]
      --initial-load <HOW>      Whether the pager waits for images before it shows the document
                                [possible values: wait, background]
      --passthrough <HOW>       Whether kitty's images pass through tmux [possible values: detect,
                                none, tmux]
      --front-matter <STYLE>    How to show the front matter [possible values: table, code, hide,
                                off]
      --headings <HOW>          How headings show [possible values: auto, sized, images, plain]
      --table-rows <STYLE>      Table row style [possible values: off, zebra, lines, indent,
                                underline]
      --diagrams <SWITCH>       Whether to draw diagrams and formulas [possible values: on, off]
      --diagram-timeout <SECS>  How long a program may take to draw one diagram, in seconds
      --diagram-panel <SWITCH>  Whether a diagram in the other page's colours lies on a panel
                                [possible values: on, off]
      --render-errors <WHERE>   Where to tell why a diagram could not be drawn [possible values:
                                inline, stderr, both]
      --no-mouse                Leave the mouse to the terminal in the pager
      --mouse                   Let the pager take the mouse
      --reading                 Experimental: the text in a proportional font, as a browser shows it
      --no-reading              Reading mode off, whatever KIRI_READING and the configuration say
      --wide <HOW>              Experimental: wide code and tables wrap or scroll in reading mode
                                [possible values: wrap, scroll]
      --max-image-size <MB>     Largest image file to read, in megabytes [default: 10]
  -h, --help                    Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version                 Print version

Images and diagrams are drawn only in terminals that support kitty's graphics protocol with Unicode
placeholders, such as kitty 0.28 or later and Ghostty 1.0 or later; elsewhere images show their alt
text and diagrams their code.
